0.1, lr_q=0.1,\n","        num_iters=num_iters, seed=seed,\n","        log_freq=log_freq, time_limit=time_tol, utility_type = \"Cobb-Douglas\")\n","\n","leo_outputs = one_sample_sgd_fastlog(\n","        A_matrix, b_constraint, q0, valuations, budgets, p0,\n","        lr_p=0.1, lr_q=0.1,\n","        num_iters=num_iters, seed=seed,\n","        log_freq=log_freq, time_limit=time_tol, utility_type = \"Leontief\")\n","\n","# --- FINAL ALLOCATION ---\n","linear_alloc = linear_outputs[-1]\n","cd_alloc = cd_outputs[-1]\n","leo_alloc = leo_outputs[-1]"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"lO2gFrxXv03j"},"source":["### Visualization"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["**Cobb-Douglas and Leontief utilities have distinct characteristics:**\n","\n","* *Cobb-Douglas Utility*:  This function penalizes very low allocations of any single good, as a zero allocation for any item would result in zero utility. It generally encourages a balanced consumption of all goods based on their valuation weights.\n","\n","* *Leontief Utility*: This function is dictated by the bottleneck resource. Utility is limited by the minimum ratio of allocated goods to their valuation weights. It encourages allocating resources in such a way that the user can consume all goods in a fixed proportion.\n","\n","**Why they might be concurrent in this specific case:**\n","\n","For certain valuation distributions and resource constraints, the optimal way to satisfy both the balanced consumption (Cobb-Douglas) and the bottleneck-driven consumption (Leontief) can lead to very similar allocations. If, for instance, there isn't a single dominating bottleneck and a relatively balanced distribution of resources is also beneficial, both functions might guide the optimization process toward comparable solutions. The SGD algorithm, starting from the same initial conditions, would then trace similar convergence paths for both, leading to almost identical relative errors over iterations when compared to the centralized optimal solution."],"metadata":{"id":"L-rv9gTnnASU"}},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":607},"id":"3w0LemDFv2w3","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1764980071257,"user_tz":-420,"elapsed":251,"user":{"displayName":"Hong Chu","userId":"14501893030136914855"}},"outputId":"97e9b689-a8a7-40db-96ac-19fcc571d002"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 800x600 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"source":["robustness_graph(linear_outputs[-1], cd_outputs[-1], leo_outputs[-1], solver_alloc)\n","plt.savefig(\"/content/drive/MyDrive/EV_charging_project/images/robustness/10users_24items.png\")\n","plt.show()"]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# 1. Gom TẤT CẢ các biến bạn muốn lưu vào một dictionary\n","import pickle\n","all_results = {\n","    'solver_allocation': solver_alloc,\n","    'linear_allocation': linear_alloc,\n","    'cobb_douglas_allocation': cd_alloc,\n","    'leontief_allocation': leo_alloc\n","}\n","\n","# 2. Định nghĩa đường dẫn và lưu file\n","save_path_pickle = '/content/drive/MyDrive/EV_charging_project/experiment_result/robustness/10_users_24_items_allocation.pkl'\n","\n","# 'wb' nghĩa là \"write binary\" (ghi nhị phân)\n","with open(save_path_pickle, 'wb') as f:\n","    pickle.dump(all_results, f)\n","\n","print(f\"Đã lưu thành công TOÀN BỘ kết quả vào: {save_path_pickle}\")"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"HsAT9Xc60q1c","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1764980071275,"user_tz":-420,"elapsed":17,"user":{"displayName":"Hong Chu","userId":"14501893030136914855"}},"outputId":"f7a6dfa0-1654-4dd6-ad84-67d9464360c0"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Đã lưu thành công TOÀN BỘ kết quả vào: /content/drive/MyDrive/EV_charging_project/experiment_result/robustness/10_users_24_items_allocation.pkl\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id"